## Pre-Flight — Read Before Every Task

Before writing ANY code, confirm:

- [ ] I have read and understood the full scope of what is being asked
- [ ] I know which backend APIs, schemas, services, auth flows, and infra this touches
- [ ] I know the exact files I will create or modify and where each one goes per the project structure
- [ ] I have verified this will not break any existing functionality, feature, or integration
- [ ] I have checked the relevant `.cursor/skills/` for any applicable patterns before writing code

Before marking ANY task complete, verify:

- [ ] All new components are co-located (`.tsx` + `.module.css` + `.types.ts` in one folder inside `src/components/`)
- [ ] All new state logic is in `src/features/` (slice + selectors + api — no components in features/)
- [ ] No `.tsx` file exceeds 888 LOC — check with `wc -l`
- [ ] All elements are theme aware (light + dark) using CSS variables from `globals.css`
- [ ] All interactive elements are WAI-ARIA, A11y, WCAG 2+ compliant (keyboard nav, aria labels, focus management, contrast)
- [ ] ECharts use raw `echarts` package only, instance behind ref, `setOption` with `notMerge: false` for updates
- [ ] Every new user-facing action has a Cmd+K registry entry in `useCommandRegistry`
- [ ] Atomic commit made with correct local author and conventional commit prefix
- [ ] Build succeeds and all relevant containers/services are healthy
- [ ] Work item (GitHub Issue or ADO Board) updated with full traceability — PR linked, blockers documented, status current, test cases noted

If ANY box above cannot be checked, the task is NOT complete. DO NOT respond to the user until all boxes are checked.
